{title: 517 - My Faith Looks Up to Thee}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #517 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 517}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]My faith looks [A/C#]up to [D]Thee,
[A]Thou Lamb [A7]of Calvary,
[D]Savior [Em]divine;
[D]Now hear mewhile I pray,
[D]Take all myguilt [Bm]away,
[F#m]Oletme [D]from this [G]day
[D]Be wholly Thine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]May thy rich [A/C#]grace impart
[A]strength to [A7]my fainting heart,
[D]my [A/E]zeal [Em]inspire!
[D]As thou hast died for me,
[D]O may my love [Bm]to [A]thee
[F#m]pure, warm, [A7/E]and [D]changeless [A]be,
[D]a living fire!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]While life's [A/C#]dark maze I [D]tread,
[A]and griefs [A7]around me spread,
[D]be [A/E]thou [Em]my [A]guide;
[D]bid darkness turn to day,
[D]wipe sorrow's tears [Bm]away,
[F#m]nor [A7/E]let [D]me ever [A]stray
[D]from Thee aside.
{end_of_verse}
